// ts_jsx.sa -- JSX element descriptors for tsgosa mapping.
//
// Descriptor (JEV jsx_jsval_descriptor, confidence 1.0, probability 1.0;
// jsx_scope simple_only, confidence 0.98, probability 0.99):
//   A JSX element is a jsval object (kind 4) whose payload is a 24-byte
//   element struct:
//     +0: tag handle (ptr to a 16-byte str struct; intrinsic tag name, or
//         component name as a string only -- component identity is NOT a
//         function reference; DOM semantics are NOT claimed)
//     +8: props handle (ptr to a btree_map with jsval values; empty map
//         when there are no attributes)
//     +16: children handle (ptr to a jsval box of kind 5, whose payload is
//         a thin array of jsval child handles; empty array when no children)
//   The jsval box itself follows the ts_jsval layout (32 bytes, +0 kind,
//   +8 payload, +16 zero, +24 zero sidecar).
// Ownership: caller owns the returned jsval box; tag/props/children handles
// are stored into the element struct and must NOT be released by the caller
// after the call (transfer into the descriptor, same discipline as
// object-literal fields stored into an inst). The helper allocates the
// element struct and the jsval box; both escape through the returned box.
// Scope: intrinsic tags, fragments (tag ""), self-closing tags, string /
// expression attributes, text / expression children, nested elements.
// Spread attributes, member tags (Foo.Bar), namespaced tags, and event
// handler semantics are refused by the emitter, not by this helper.

// @ts_jsx_element builds a JSX element descriptor jsval from its parts
// (tag str handle, props map handle, children jsval-array box handle).
@ts_jsx_element(tag: ptr, props: ptr, children: ptr) -> ptr:
L_TJX_ENTRY:
    e = alloc 24
    store e+0, tag as ptr
    store e+8, props as ptr
    store e+16, children as ptr
    h = alloc 32
    store h+0, 4 as i32
    store h+8, e as ptr
    store h+16, 0 as i32
    store h+24, 0 as ptr
    return h
